        "title": "AFTD2022-EXP-6c3afdfbb9a8da76 | In managing impaired hypoglycaemia awareness, the medical practitioner should focus on aspects of the person’s self-care to minimise a severe hypoglycaemic event occurring while driving, including steps described above (Advice to drivers). In addition, self-care behaviours that help to minimise severe hypoglycaemic events in general should be a major ongoing focus of regular diabetes care. This requires attention by both the medical practitioner and the person with diabetes to diet and exercise approaches, insulin regimens and blood glucose testing protocols.",
